BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fcc85d13a4bde9c2299836f6@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260904T180719Z
SUMMARY:GREY GARDENS (1975)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Browning Cinema Sunday Docs Directed by Ellen Hovde\, Albert Ma
 ysles\, David Maysles\, Muffie Meyer With Little Edie Bouvier Beale\, Edi
 th Bouvier Beale\, Brooks Hyers Rated PG\, 94 minutes\, DCP Meet Big and 
 Little Edie Beale: mother and daughter\, high-society dropouts\, and recl
 usive cousins of Jackie Onassis. The two manage to thrive together (with 
 the help of some raccoons) amid the decay and disorder of their East Hamp
 ton\, New York\, mansion\, making for an eerily ramshackle echo of the Am
 erican Camelot. An impossibly intimate portrait\, this 1976 documentary b
 y Albert and David Maysles\, codirected by Ellen Hovde and Muffie Meyer\,
  quickly became a cult classic and established Little Edie as a fashion i
 con and philosopher queen. Sponsored by the Meg and John P. Brogan Endowm
 ent for Documentary Film.\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/ev
 ents/grey-gardens-1975/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/grey-gardens-1975/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260906T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260906T173000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
